

Loan Approval and Risk Analysis System


Project Overview
This project analyzes loan applicant data to improve credit risk assessment, loan approval decisions, and financial stability evaluation.
It uses SQL, Pandas, Power BI, and Matplotlib/Seaborn to extract insights and build a decision-support system.

SQL Tasks
* Loan approval distribution (Approved vs Rejected)
* Risk segmentation using CIBIL score
* Previous default vs approval analysis
* Average income vs loan amount
* Loan approval by lender type
* Rejection reason analysis

Derived Metrics
* Loan-to-Income Ratio (LTI)
* EMI-to-Income Ratio
* Debt-to-Income Ratio (DTI)

Pandas Tasks
* Data cleaning and preprocessing
* Handling missing values
* Feature engineering (Risk category, LTI, DTI)
* Exploratory data analysis (EDA)
* Behavioral analysis of applicants

Power BI Tasks
* Loan approval vs rejection visualization
* Risk category vs approval charts
* Income vs loan amount analysis
* Rejection reason dashboard

KPI Cards
* Total applications
* Approval rate
* Average income
* Average loan amount

Matplotlib & Seaborn Tasks
* Histogram of income distribution
* Boxplot of loan amount vs approval
* Correlation heatmap
* Scatterplot (Income vs Loan)
* Bar charts for rejection reasons


Project Workflow
1. Data extraction using SQL
2. Data cleaning and processing using Pandas
3. Data visualization using Matplotlib and Seaborn
4. Dashboard creation using Power BI


Key Outcomes
* Identified key factors affecting loan approval
* Built risk segmentation logic
* Developed financial health indicators
* Created interactive dashboard


Conclusion
This project transforms raw loan data into actionable insights, enabling data-driven decision-making in credit risk assessment.
